  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Narration says he is merely twenty-eight years old and a clan elite from Tie clan’s side branch. Many people tried to recruit him, but he decided to serve Tie Ruo Nan instead, and is only one of the talented elites she has recruited into her faction.",
      "chapters": [
        302
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_tie_clan",
        "char_tie_ruo_nan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He has a delicate face.",
      "chapters": [
        302
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Tie Xian Hua is sent flying and throws up huge amounts of blood, Tie Mu rushes over, holds her, and promptly begins healing her while rattan shell grass soldiers defend them.",
      "chapters": [
        360
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "healing-tie-xian-hua",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tie_xian_hua"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "While healing Tie Xian Hua he says Little Beast King is terrifying and that their side still cannot catch him. After her injuries are healed and she has strength to fight again, he adds from beside her that Fang Zheng cannot escape even if he grows wings. When Fang Yuan then does fly, Tie Mu is baffled that his words turned into a prophecy.",
      "chapters": [
        361
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_little_beast_king",
        "char_fang_zheng",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later Fang Yuan pounces from the air. Others shout for Tie Mu to be careful. Fang Yuan grabs his shoulders, tears both arms from the shoulders, then smacks his hands and bursts Tie Mu’s head open. The Tie clan group sees his death with furious eyes.",
      "chapters": [
        361
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tie Xian Hua shouts that Fang Yuan killed Tie Mu and that she wants him dead. Narration later lists Tie Mu, Tie Xian Hua, and Tie Dao Ku as all having died in Fang Yuan’s hands.",
      "chapters": [
        362
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "named-among-the-fallen",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tie_dao_ku"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Months later Tie Ruo Nan faces tombstones that name Tie Mu, Tie Dao Ku, Tie Xian Hua, Tie Ao Kai, and Tie Ba Xiu. Tie Mu Bai tells her Tie clansmen are buried where they die, and names Tie Mu among those for whom dying on the battlefield is the greatest honor.",
      "chapters": [
        369
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "tombstones-and-burial-honor",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tie_ao_kai",
        "char_tie_ba_xiu",
        "char_tie_mu_bai"
      ]
    }
  ],
